mammal|animal|NOUN|Milk-producing animal|An animal of the group whose mothers feed their young with milk.|động vật có vú|A whale is a mammal, not a fish.|Cá voi là động vật có vú, không phải cá.|Countable; egg-laying exceptions exist.|-
ironically|unexpected|ADVERB|Contrary to expectation|Used when a result contrasts strikingly with what was expected.|trớ trêu thay|Ironically, the rain began just after we packed the umbrellas.|Trớ trêu thay, mưa bắt đầu ngay sau khi chúng tôi cất ô.|Sentence adverb.|0
ironically|tone|ADVERB|With ironic meaning|In a way that suggests the opposite of the words' literal meaning.|một cách mỉa mai|He called the long wait delightful, ironically.|Anh ấy gọi quãng chờ dài là thú vị, với giọng mỉa mai.|Manner adverb; tone depends on context.|-
monetary|money|ADJECTIVE|Relating to money|Connected with money.|liên quan đến tiền; tiền tệ|The award carries no monetary value.|Giải thưởng không có giá trị tiền tệ.|Attributive adjective.|-
invalid|not-valid|ADJECTIVE|Not valid|Not acceptable or effective because a rule or requirement is not met.|không hợp lệ; không có hiệu lực|The machine rejected the invalid ticket.|Máy từ chối chiếc vé không hợp lệ.|Invalid document or argument; adjective stress differs from noun.|-
jealous|envy|ADJECTIVE|Envious of an advantage|Unhappy because someone has something you want.|ghen tị|He was jealous of his friend's new bicycle.|Anh ấy ghen tị với chiếc xe đạp mới của bạn.|Jealous of.|-
jealous|relationship|ADJECTIVE|Afraid of losing affection|Upset because you fear someone you love prefers another person.|ghen tuông|She felt jealous when her partner praised a former girlfriend.|Cô ấy thấy ghen khi bạn đời khen bạn gái cũ.|Relationship jealousy; no endorsement of control.|-
